  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 358 PM CDT Wed Oct 28 2026\n\nStill continue to expect an active weather pattern setting up \nheading into the weekend and early next week. A shortwave trof \nwill move in Friday, with increasing moisture out ahead of the \ntrof, will see the potential for rain showers and maybe an \nisolated chance for a thunderstorm late Friday afternoon into \nFriday overnight, before tapering Saturday morning. Expect \nSaturday afternoon and evening to remain mostly dry before focus\nturns on the next system. Still continue to see discrepancies \nbetween the models with one model brining in the system as more \nof a stronger closed low and the other bringing it in more open \nwave. Continue to have low confidence in this time as to the \nexact track of the storm, but the potential exist for gusty \nwinds and precipitation late Sunday through Tuesday.",
